// expect-error: cannot assign to '.len' of an array
// BUG-967: the ARRAY sibling. An array's `.len` is a compile-time constant, so this
// emitted `_zer_t0 = 4U = 100ULL;` — invalid C that only GCC rejected. Loud drift
// rather than the slice case's silent out-of-bounds write, but the same question,
// and answered by the same query rather than a second rule that could drift.
u32 main() {
    u8[4] a;
    a.len = 100;
    return 0;
}
